    "solution": "From the lower approach, turn the upright arm right before entering the left prism. With gravity inverted, cross from the small ceiling island onto the underside of the horizontal arm. At its hub, move to the outside before turning it down: the former ceiling becomes a wall descending toward the far prism. Climb its other face downward, pass the second prism, and take the lower-right tally. Return up the same vertical arm under ordinary gravity, turn it left to restore a westward bridge, and return above the first prism to the opened western loft. On returning from the tally, jump through the low prism without dashing; dash only after clearing it to keep normal gravity. The little island used as a ceiling on the outward trip is now a landing to climb over on the final return.",
